.Language=English,English (English)
.PluginContents=File list creator (Dir2File)

@Contents
$^#File list creator (Dir2File)#

      This module allows you to generate a file list containing records
for each object matching search criteria specified. The records are created
on the basis of templates which (hopefully) you have already used as S&R
"replacement strings". The module will only work in Far 1.70 build 1634 and
above. To avoid unnecessary redundancy, this help file does not contain
information, which consists in standard ~Search and Replace (S&R)~@<..\..\>@ plugin
documentation.

      Using this plugin you may view lots of pictures in your favourite
browser, process multiple archives (e.g. rar, zip and arj at the same time),
merge #Favourites# (and other url-files) into one html-page, rename lots of files
according to a certain rule (though renaming files is more convinient with
~newname.srp~@<..\NewName\>Contents@), find out versions of files and lots more.
Virtually unlimited functionality may even scare you if you're new to this plugin :)


^#Dialog description:#

      Some options and buttons are similar to those in the parent plugin
~Search and Replace~@<..\..\>MainDialog@.

      If #Search in selected# is checked and #Process subfolders# is disabled, then
selected folders will be processed according to their own template just like ordinary
files.

  #Enter name#        Records are to be placed into this file.
  #of file#
  #to create#

  #First line#        It is written at the beginning of the output file
                    before processing starts. It is a
                    ~regular expression~@<..\..\>RegExp@ for replacement
                    string.

  #Last line#         This line is appended to the end of the output
                    file after processing has been finished. It is a
                    ~regular expression~@<..\..\>ReplaceRegExp@ for replacement string.

      Below you will find description of options for several groups of
objects (four groups of files and folders options).
They are the following:

  #Type#              It is a ~file mask~@<..\..\>FileMask@. If the found object
  #(file-mask)#       matches the mask, it is associated with the
                    group for the mask.

  #Search template#   It is applied to file name. It's a ~regular~@<..\..\>RegExp@
                    ~expression~@<..\..\>RegExp@ for search string. The result of
                    template and file name comparison may be used in
                    replace template (i.e. you can refer to brackets
                    found by this expression). You may leave this
                    field empty. It is necessity to enclose the
                    ~search string~@<..\..\>RegExp@ in slashes: #/#regexp#/#options.

  #Replace template#  A ~regular expression~@<..\..\>ReplaceRegExp@ for replacement
                    string. Its result is written in the target
                    output file.

      Additional settings:

  #Codepage #         This button allows you to choose any codepage
  #of the output#     installed in FAR.
  #file#

  #Initiate value#    This option affects the next
  #of the counter#    replacement string ~regexp~@<..\..\>ReplaceRegExp@- counter (#\###).
  #by zero...#

  #Common counter#    If this option is disabled, each replace template
                    will have its own independent
                    ~counter~@<..\..\>ReplaceRegExp@. Otherwise the counter will
                    be shared by all of the 5 output templates.

  #Scheme#            Calls scheme management dialog.
                    Use #Alt-Shift-0#...#Alt-Shift-9# for quick
                    switching between first 10 schemes.

  #Save#              Save current settings as a scheme
                    (you will be prompted to enter scheme name).

      See also #Reg\dir2file_scheme.reg# - it contains several
examples of schemes.
